0 0 0 125 500 0 0-125z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Autoscale" data-attr="zoom" data-val="auto" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m250 850l-187 0-63 0 0-62 0-188 63 0 0 188 187 0 0 62z m688 0l-188 0 0-62 188 0 0-188 62 0 0 188 0 62-62 0z m-875-938l0 188-63 0 0-188 0-62 63 0 187 0 0 62-187 0z m875 188l0-188-188 0 0-62 188 0 62 0 0 62 0 188-62 0z m-125 188l-1 0-93-94-156 156 156 156 92-93 2 0 0 250-250 0 0-2 93-92-156-156-156 156 94 92 0 2-250 0 0-250 0 0 93 93 157-156-157-156-93 94 0 0 0-250 250 0 0 0-94 93 156 157 156-157-93-93 0 0 250 0 0 250z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div><div class="modebar-group"><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Toggle Spike Lines" data-attr="_cartesianSpikesEnabled" data-val="on" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="M512 409c0-57-46-104-103-104-57 0-104 47-104 104 0 57 47 103 104 103 57 0 103-46 103-103z m-327-39l92 0 0 92-92 0z m-185 0l92 0 0 92-92 0z m370-186l92 0 0 93-92 0z m0-184l92 0 0 92-92 0z" transform="matrix(1.5 0 0 -1.5 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Show closest data on hover" data-attr="hovermode" data-val="closest" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="ne"><svg viewBox="0 0 1500 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m375 725l0 0-375-375 375-374 0-1 1125 0 0 750-1125 0z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn active" data-title="Compare data on hover" data-attr="hovermode" data-val="x" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="ne"><svg viewBox="0 0 1125 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m187 786l0 2-187-188 188-187 0 0 937 0 0 373-938 0z m0-499l0 1-187-188 188-188 0 0 937 0 0 376-938-1z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div><div class="modebar-group"><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Save plot as PNG" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="m500 450c-83 0-150-67-150-150 0-83 67-150 150-150 83 0 150 67 150 150 0 83-67 150-150 150z m400 150h-120c-16 0-34 13-39 29l-31 93c-6 15-23 28-40 28h-340c-16 0-34-13-39-28l-31-94c-6-15-23-28-40-28h-120c-55 0-100-45-100-100v-450c0-55 45-100 100-100h800c55 0 100 45 100 100v450c0 55-45 100-100 100z m-400-550c-138 0-250 112-250 250 0 138 112 250 250 250 138 0 250-112 250-250 0-138-112-250-250-250z m365 380c-19 0-35-16-35-35 0-19 16-35 35-35 19 0 35 16 35 35 0 19-16 35-35 35z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a><a rel="tooltip" class="modebar-btn" data-title="Open in dialog (edit layout)" data-toggle="false" data-gravity="n"><svg viewBox="0 0 1000 1000" class="icon" height="1em" width="1em"><path d="M786 296v-267q0-15-11-26t-25-10h-214v214h-143v-214h-214q-15 0-25 10t-11 26v267q0 1 0 2t0 2l321 264 321-264q1-1 1-4z m124 39l-34-41q-5-5-12-6h-2q-7 0-12 3l-386 322-386-322q-7-4-13-4-7 2-12 7l-35 41q-4 5-3 13t6 12l401 334q18 15 42 15t43-15l136-114v109q0 8 5 13t13 5h107q8 0 13-5t5-13v-227l122-102q5-5 6-12t-4-13z" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 850)"></path></svg></a></div></div></div><svg class="main-svg" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" width="994" height="494"><g class="hoverlayer"></g></svg></div></div></div></foreignObject></g><g transform="translate(660,20)" x="660" y="20" title="codeHTML" width="560" height="346" class="codeHTML" name="codeHTML" rot="0"><foreignObject x="0" y="0" width="560" height="346" style="width: 560px; height: 346px;"><div name="htmlCode" style="zoom: 0.56; height: 617.857px; width: 1000px;" code="&lt;div class=&quot;ch&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Hartley oscillator&lt;/h1&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;ch-card&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;How it works&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The tank circuit is made of the &lt;strong&gt;tapped inductor L1 + L2&lt;/strong&gt; and the capacitor &lt;strong&gt;C1&lt;/strong&gt;. The &lt;strong&gt;tap&lt;/strong&gt; (the junction of L1 and L2) is connected to the supply, which is an AC ground.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The collector of &lt;strong&gt;Q1&lt;/strong&gt; is connected to one end of the tank (through L1, which also gives the DC supply), and the base is connected to the other end through &lt;strong&gt;Cb&lt;/strong&gt;. The two ends of a tapped coil are in opposite phase and so is the common-emitter transistor: the feedback is positive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The feedback ratio is set by the taps &lt;code&gt;L1 / L2&lt;/code&gt;. The oscillation grows until the transistor limits the amplitude.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Frequency&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;f = 1 / (2&amp;pi; &amp;radic;((L1 + L2) &amp;middot; C1))&lt;/code&gt; = 1 / (2&amp;pi; &amp;radic;(200 &amp;micro;H &amp;middot; 1 nF)) &amp;asymp; 356 kHz&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In the PyAMS simulation: about 352 kHz.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Circuit&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;V1&lt;/strong&gt; = 12 V. &lt;strong&gt;Q1&lt;/strong&gt;: model &lt;code&gt;BJT&lt;/code&gt; (NPN). &lt;strong&gt;R1&lt;/strong&gt; = 220 k&amp;Omega; sets the base current, &lt;strong&gt;RE&lt;/strong&gt; = 1 k&amp;Omega; limits the gain (and the amplitude).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;L1&lt;/strong&gt; = &lt;strong&gt;L2&lt;/strong&gt; = 100 &amp;micro;H, &lt;strong&gt;C1&lt;/strong&gt; = 1 nF, &lt;strong&gt;Cb&lt;/strong&gt; = 10 nF.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;C1 has an initial voltage&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;Ic&lt;/code&gt; = 1 V): it starts the oscillation, as the noise does in a real circuit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Time domain analysis: 0 ... 400 &amp;micro;s with a step of 20 ns. Plotted: the collector &lt;code&gt;a&lt;/code&gt; and the other end of the tank &lt;code&gt;k&lt;/code&gt;. The amplitude settles after about 300 &amp;micro;s.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The coils are not magnetically coupled (as in the simplest Hartley oscillator). The drawing in the picture of the oscillator is simplified: here the tap is connected to the supply and no RFC is needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
"> 
